# Engine wave E3. On the fork, list.equals(other) did not compile for an ArrayList, a List.of(...), an array, a
# StringBuilder, an Object or a program's own class: "reference to equals is ambiguous: both method
# equals(java.lang.Object) in java.lang.Object and method equals(java.lang.Object) in java.lang.Object match" (in
# java.util.AbstractList for the lists). HashSet's and TreeSet's clone() failed the same way ("reference to clone
# is ambiguous"). The pinned JDK compiles each and prints what the E3 cases record (runtime/test/cases.mjs): true
# and false for equal and unequal lists, StringBuilders and objects, false for two arrays with the same contents
# (an array's equals is identity), and a copy from clone() that equals the set it came from.
#   - teavm-javac-0103 exports a method TeaVM declares under another name plus @Rename under its JDK name. TObject
#     and TAbstractList declare equals(Object) and also @Rename("equals") equals0(TObject); THashSet and TTreeSet
#     declare clone() and @Rename("clone") clone0(), which returns TObject. 0103's guard leaves a rename out when
#     the class declares the new name with the original descriptor, but here the descriptors differ until TeaVM's
#     class names are renamed (TObject to Object). Renamed, equals0 became a second equals(Object) in the compile
#     classlib's java.lang.Object and java.util.AbstractList, and clone0 a second clone() in HashSet and TreeSet, so
#     javac found two methods for every call that reached them. Types that override equals (String, Integer,
#     Character, Double, HashSet, HashMap, records) compiled before and still do (E3-equals-overriding-types).
#   - Now, before a class is converted, every renamed method whose new name plus renamed descriptor the stub
#     already has is left out: one declared under its own name (kept, in whatever order the class declares them)
#     or another renamed method written before it. The stub then declares each method once. Nothing changes at
#     run time: the stub is the compile classlib, which javac reads for names and types only.
#
# Written from teavm-javac's own source (compiler/src/main/java/org/teavm/javac/StdlibConverter.java), TeaVM's
# classlib (TObject.java, TAbstractList.java, THashSet.java, TTreeSet.java and the other @Rename sites) and the
# pinned JDK's observed output; no OpenJDK source was opened (clean room, D14). Written by a subagent (Claude Opus
# 5.5), a language model whose training may include OpenJDK, so the patch was read for names or structure that
# look recalled rather than derived: it adds one field and one method of the converter's own, reusing 0103's
# renames map and the converter's renameMethodDesc.
#
# Applies to: github.com/konsoletyper/teavm-javac 2ddcf02e (master, 2026-09-04), after teavm-javac-0101 to
# teavm-javac-0103, with or without teavm-javac-0104 to 0106, which change other lines of the same file. It changes
# lines teavm-javac-0103 wrote (the renames field, visitMethod's rename and addFile), so it cannot apply without
# 0103, and the leave-one-out build without 0103 leaves it out too (runtime/build.sh and runtime/test/negatives.mjs
# read the line below).
# Builds on: teavm-javac-0103

diff --git a/compiler/src/main/java/org/teavm/javac/StdlibConverter.java b/compiler/src/main/java/org/teavm/javac/StdlibConverter.java
index 74ec518..b8db19a 100644
